WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.680
- The Britney Spears conservatorship case

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.810
keeps getting more interesting
and more interesting.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.420
Most recently, her
longtime manager has left

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:07.590
and he was followed

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.920
by her longtime court-appointed
lawyer, Samuel Ingram.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.040
Now there are times when
a lawyer must resign

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.320
from representing their client,

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.790
but that probably doesn't apply here.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.890
Things like your client
has asked you to do things

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:18.900
that are illegal

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.860
or you're a witness in
the actual case itself.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.270
What's more likely here is that Ingram,

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.670
based on the notoriety from this case

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.680
and a slew of articles

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.620
that don't paint him in a
particularly great light,

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.960
feels that he can no
longer represent Spears.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.640
And there may or may not
be anything untoward here.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.600
Now in a case where a
lawyer wants to withdraw,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.820
they generally have to get
approval from the court.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.630
The court has to make
sure that this withdrawal

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.960
doesn't prejudice their client.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.750
So ironically, we'll see both Brittany

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.553
and her lawyer in court.

